# Vamp OS: BusyBox init (docs/vamp-os-base.md#what-boots). rcS brings up the kernel's file systems, /dev,
# /mnt/data, the modules, the framebuffer and the input devices; only then does init start runsvdir, which
# starts each service in /etc/sv and starts it again when it ends. No login on the serial port and root locked,
# as in today's Vamp (tools/build.py SERIAL_GETTY); the kernel's and init's messages still reach the console.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::respawn:/usr/bin/runsvdir -P /etc/sv
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcK
::restart:/sbin/init
